WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.770
Hey Wisecrack, Jared here, and today we’re
talking about the smart and stylish JRPG that

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:17.000
lets you simultaneously date your high school
teacher, your middle school-aged step-sister,

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.640
and an alcoholic Lois Lane: Persona 5.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:23.870
For those of you who’ve never played Persona
5, we recommend pausing this video and playing

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.350
through the 120 hour campaign.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:29.140
But if you don’t have that much time, we’ll
summarize it for you.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:33.440
The Persona series is basically what you’d
get if a group of otaku made a Pokemon clone

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.030
set in the world of Inside Out.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:39.030
You spend half the game in a high school social
management simulator, and the other half as

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:43.760
a superhero gentleman thief that enters people’s
cognitions in order to catch ‘em all, albeit

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.559
instead of Pikachus you’re nabbing mythological
monsters, gods, heroes, historical figures,

00:00:48.559 --> 00:00:52.120
and characters from literature - including
whatever the hell this is.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:56.480
Going by the codename Joker, you slowly assemble
a crew called the Phantom Thieves of Hearts

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:01.269
to heist the innermost desires from the most
powerful and corrupt adults in society.

00:01:01.269 --> 00:01:05.940
- “You sons of bitches - what’s the job?”

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:10.680
So let’s look at whether the aspects of
Persona which people praise so often are actually

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.200
Deep or Dumb.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.800
Spoilers ahead for the original game, but
not for the expanded Persona 5 Royal which

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:57.180
won’t be available state side until the end of March.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.599
Part 1 - Jungian Psychology

00:02:02.599 --> 00:02:05.600
Carl Jung was the founder of analytical psychology.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:10.560
Just as his colleague Sigmund Freud invented
an entire vocabulary for psychoanalysis, Jung

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:15.340
coined terms like archetype, shadow, persona,
and the collective unconscious and the series

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:17.990
cites its Jungian influences explicitly.

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:23.310
In Persona 4 Golden, you can unlock new episodes
of Mr. Edogawa's TV Classroom, which are straight

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.670
up lectures about Jungian psychology.

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:29.940
But the primary place you encounter these
Jungian terms is during the combat sections.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:33.750
When our regular high schoolers enter the
Metaverse, they transform into personas that

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:38.400
are dramatizations of the Jungian concept
much in the same way as Joy and Anger in Inside

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.540
Out are dramatizations of emotions.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:45.630
Really, the whole world of Persona is a dramatization
of Jung’s ideas about the human psyche.

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:49.580
Take the Metaverse, a world created by human
cognition that the Phantom Thieves are capable

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:50.580
of entering.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:56.080
The Metaverse is representative of all psychological
activity, collective and individual, conscience

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:57.490
and unconscious.

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:02.850
Some parts, called Palaces, represent an individual’s
mental activity, specifically their distorted

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:05.230
perspective of a place in the real world.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:07.220
Take the girl’s volleyball coach, Kamoshida.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:11.500
He’s got such a high opinion of his status
at Shujin Academy that he envisions it as

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.420
a castle, ruled by him as its king.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:19.700
Other parts, such as Mementos, are how society
as a whole sees the world around it, and given

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:23.270
the deep cynicism of the day, it’s not a
pleasant place.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:27.550
This shared psychic space of society, along
with the Sea of Souls from which all Shadows

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:32.400
and Personas emerge, are dramatizations of
a Jungian concept called the Collective Unconscious.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:37.459
It’s those parts of the mind that we inherited
from our most remote ancestors, like fight

00:03:37.459 --> 00:03:38.459
or flight.

00:03:38.459 --> 00:03:42.681
But it also includes what Jung described as
“pre-existent forms, the archetypes... which

00:03:42.681 --> 00:03:45.680
give definite form to certain psychic contents.”

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:50.950
Of the innumerable archetypes within the Collective
Unconscious, Jung considered four to be primordial,

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:56.340
the most basic and universal images, among
which are the Persona and the Shadow.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:59.430
Personas are social masks that the Ego chooses
to wear.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:03.150
Jung himself described them as “designed
on the one hand to make a definite impression

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:07.500
upon others, and, on the other, to conceal
the true nature of the individual.”

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:10.970
In Latin, persona refers to the masks worn
by actors.

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:14.709
In the game, whenever they enter the Metaverse,
the Phantom Thieves quite literally wear their

00:04:14.709 --> 00:04:16.470
Personas as masks.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:21.380
Per Jung, the Thieves’ Personas are how
they want society to see them, and how they

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:22.940
want to see themselves.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:27.220
Take Ann, who is apprehensive about her beauty
because it draws unwanted attention.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:31.880
When her Persona awakens, it’s as Carmen
from the famous opera, a fierce femme fatale

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:35.020
who uses her penchant for seduction to deadly
effect.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:39.790
Effectively, this transforms Ann’s appearance
from a liability into a strength.

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:44.560
Another Jungian term is Shadow or the psychological
aspects which the conscience self is unaware

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:46.770
of and would rather not acknowledge.

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:49.160
In the game, Shadows serve as the enemies.

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:52.680
Most are generic, but the bosses are Shadows
specific to certain characters.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.830
But the game designers didn’t just look
to Jung for their worldbuilding.

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:59.760
His ideas are equally represented in the gameplay
mechanics as well.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:03.510
The way Shadows and Personas are grouped reflects
Jung’s conception of archetypes.

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:08.290
Per Jung, “The term 'archetype' is often
misunderstood as meaning certain definite

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:10.460
mythological images or motifs, but.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:15.160
... The archetype is a tendency to form such
representations of a motif—representations

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:19.250
that can vary a great deal in detail without
losing their basic pattern.”

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:23.780
So the Personas aren’t themselves part of
the Collective Unconscious that everyone inherits.

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:26.470
No one is born with the idea of Odin in their
head.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:30.550
But they do have part of their mental space
sequestered off for the idea of Senex, the

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:35.530
generic Wise Old Man, and this idea is given
form through characters such as Odin, Baal,

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:39.260
and Thoth, who are all grouped together in
the game’s organization.

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:43.020
To capture a Shadow, Joker must find some
point of commonality with it.

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:46.180
That is, he must recognize it as being a part
of himself.

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:51.300
Similarly confronting and recognizing one's
own shadows is a distinctive aspect of Jung’s

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.310
process of individuation.

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:56.290
Once he’s moved it from the dark parts of
his psyche into the light of consciousness,

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:59.210
Joker can then equip that Shadow as a Persona.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:04.080
But there’s another gameplay use for Personas
that better exemplifies the Jungian concept.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:09.060
As Joker converses with important people called
Confidants - his bond with them strengthens.

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:13.139
Each of these has a particular archetype that
most closely exemplifies their personality.

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:17.340
By equipping a Persona belonging to the same
archetype before conversing with a Confidant,

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:22.020
Joker forges his friendship with them faster
since they’re recognizing something of themselves

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:23.020
in him.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:27.050
This is reflective of Jung’s idea that we
wear different personas for different people,

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:30.889
choosing to share one side of ourselves with
friends, another with family, and another

00:06:30.889 --> 00:06:32.280
with coworkers.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:35.540
Even more Jungian is the Phantom Thieves entire
modus operandi.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:39.889
They enter their mark’s psyche and steal
whatever the individual treasures so much

00:06:39.889 --> 00:06:44.400
that it’s twisted their desires and distorted
their perception of reality, and always end

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:46.770
up confronting the target’s Shadow.

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:50.600
After this treasure is stolen and the Shadow
defeated, the individual undergoes a dramatic

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:52.150
change of personality.

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:54.389
This can be seen as akin to psychotherapy.

00:06:54.389 --> 00:06:58.729
Despite stylizing themselves as thieves, their
goal is to effect psychological and moral

00:06:58.729 --> 00:07:03.360
improvement in the subject, albeit less talking
on a couch to defeat inner demons and more

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.850
slashing them with samurai swords.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:09.560
Given all of this - the consonance between
the worldbuilding, story, and the gameplay

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:14.870
mechanics all around this one unifying motif
- we’ve absolutely got to give Persona’s

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:18.190
use of Jungian Psychology a certified “Deep.”

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:20.620
Part 2 - Esoteric Tarot

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:24.820
The game continues its Jungian motifs with
the use of the Tarot to organize elements

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:29.960
such as Shadows, Personas, and Confidants
according to the archetypes found in the cards.

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:34.639
Jung himself acknowledged the Tarot as containing
compelling archetypal imagery: He wrote, “It

00:07:34.639 --> 00:07:38.830
also seems as if the set of pictures in the
tarot cards were distantly descended from

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:40.830
the archetypes of transformation…”

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:44.479
Tarot began back in the 15th century as a
deck for playing card games.

00:07:44.479 --> 00:07:48.949
In addition to the traditional four suits
- a.k.a. the Minor Arcana - it included twenty-two

00:07:48.949 --> 00:07:50.840
trump cards - the Major Arcana.

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:55.539
It wasn’t until the late 18th century that
it began to be used for occult purposes, of

00:07:55.539 --> 00:08:00.270
which you’re probably most familiar with
Cartomancy, or divining the future by drawing

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:01.270
cards.

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:04.710
But apart from fortune telling, the tarot
was also incorporated into occult schools

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:08.860
of thought, with each card taking on multitudes
of meaning, such as each of the Major Arcana

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:13.039
corresponding to one of the twenty-two letters
of the Hebrew alphabet and the twenty-two

00:08:13.039 --> 00:08:17.240
paths in the Kabbalah’s Tree of Life, or
the four suits of the Minor Arcana corresponding

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:21.080
to the four classical elements and the four
letters of the tetragrammaton.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:25.610
The use of the Tarot as a set of symbols became
known as Esoteric Tarot, to distinguish it

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:28.080
from its primary purpose as playing cards.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:33.350
The order of the Major Arcana also tells a
story, known as the Fool’s Journey, that

00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:37.660
is seen as both the story of each individual
soul and the history of the universe as a

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:38.709
whole.

00:08:38.709 --> 00:08:43.300
Persona 5’s most successful application
of Esoteric Tarot is in structuring its Confidants

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:45.540
system around the Fool’s Journey.

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:49.869
Joker’s own journey begins when he meets
Igor, the Confidant associated with Arcana

00:08:49.869 --> 00:08:52.149
0, “Le Meat,” a.k.a.

00:08:52.149 --> 00:08:53.149
The Fool.

00:08:53.149 --> 00:08:57.800
In Esoteric Tarot, The Fool is at the first
step on a path towards self-realization, with

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:01.730
that path taking him through the subsequent
cards of the Major Arcana.

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:05.899
This is reflected in Joker’s need to maximize
his rank with all of his Confidants - each

00:09:05.899 --> 00:09:10.459
of whom is explicitly linked to one of the
Major Arcana, and whose own side-story teaches

00:09:10.459 --> 00:09:12.829
Joker the lessons of their associated card.

00:09:12.829 --> 00:09:15.620
It’s not enough for him to simply beat the
final boss.

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:20.199
Like The Fool, he has to achieve enlightenment
in the way prescribed by Esoteric Tarot in

00:09:20.199 --> 00:09:22.600
order to unlock the game’s True Ending.

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:26.819
Which Arcana the Confidants belong to often
reflects the role they play in the narrative.

00:09:26.819 --> 00:09:30.939
Occasionally the game makes a particularly
appropriate connection regarding what Arcana

00:09:30.939 --> 00:09:34.269
a character belongs to and which Persona they
manifest.

00:09:34.269 --> 00:09:39.370
Makoto’s Arcana is “Le Papesse,” traditionally
associated with the legendary Pope Joan, the

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:42.819
very same as Makoto’s initial Persona, Johanna.

00:09:42.819 --> 00:09:47.029
But more often the game makes a surface level
association between a character’s Arcana

00:09:47.029 --> 00:09:48.370
and their personality.

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:52.959
Ann’s Arcana is “L'Amoureux” (the Lovers),
primarily because she is the first love interest

00:09:52.959 --> 00:09:56.690
available in the game and the object of desire
to multiple male characters.

00:09:56.690 --> 00:10:00.649
Futaba of “L'Ermite” literally hermits
herself away in her room.

00:10:00.649 --> 00:10:04.949
Chihaya of the “Roue de Fortune” is herself
a tarot reading fortune teller.

00:10:04.949 --> 00:10:09.380
And Tae Takemi’s work in the medical field
places her in proximity to death (her’s

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:12.470
being the card with no name, a.k.a. “La
Mort”).

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:16.899
This last one reveals how Atlus’s understanding
of Esoteric Tarot can be a bit shallow.

00:10:16.899 --> 00:10:21.959
As the Thirteenth Arcana is associated not
with literal death but is rather symbolic

00:10:21.959 --> 00:10:24.060
of endings and change.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:27.999
In some cases the surface level connection
comes at the cost of a deeper one.

00:10:27.999 --> 00:10:32.569
Haru’s final Persona, Astarte (of the Empress
Arcana), is specifically called “the Queen

00:10:32.569 --> 00:10:34.239
of Heaven in the Bible.”

00:10:34.239 --> 00:10:38.750
This naturally compares her with Mary, whom
the Catholics affirm is the Regina Coeli - the

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:39.870
Queen of Heaven.

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:45.050
However, Arthur Edward Waite - who co-created
the most famous Esoteric Tarot deck - contrasts

00:10:45.050 --> 00:10:49.230
the Empress with Mary as the Queen of Heaven,
saying the empress is associated with Mary

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:54.899
only as Refugium Peccatorum - the Refuge of
Sinners and an earthly Garden of Eden.

00:10:54.899 --> 00:10:58.959
According to him The Empress is very specifically
not a heavenly figure.

00:10:58.959 --> 00:11:01.060
The game gets it backwards.

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:03.339
This is hardly nitpicking.

00:11:03.339 --> 00:11:07.949
Esoteric Tarot is interesting specifically
because its imagery and structure invite systemization

00:11:07.949 --> 00:11:12.639
with diverse schools of thought like the Jewish
Kabbalah and the Catholic corpus doctrinae.

00:11:12.639 --> 00:11:16.600
In getting the meanings mixed-up, Persona
5 doesn’t quite justify structuring its

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:18.209
systems around the Tarot.

00:11:18.209 --> 00:11:22.709
The game is obviously interested in Tarot
for its esoteric associations as well as its

00:11:22.709 --> 00:11:27.420
Jungian ones, but fails to engage with the
esotericism in any real meaningful ways.

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:31.709
The fact that the game follows the Tarot of
Marseilles, an older deck more associated

00:11:31.709 --> 00:11:36.139
with card games, rather than the Rider-Waite
deck, which was specifically constructed to

00:11:36.139 --> 00:11:39.699
convey esoteric symbolism, certainly evidences
this.

00:11:39.699 --> 00:11:43.910
While the Fool’s Journey of the Confidants
system and one or two of the characters’

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:49.730
associated Arcana are somewhat deep, for the
most part Persona 5’s use of Tarot is kinda

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:50.910
Dumb.

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:53.850
Part 3 - Ethical Systems and Moral Realism

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:57.319
But Persona 5 is also structured to make a
moral argument.

00:11:57.319 --> 00:12:01.360
The story is built around heisting a few major
Palaces - parts of the Metaverse that have

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:04.749
been warped by the distorted perception of
a sinful individual.

00:12:04.749 --> 00:12:08.949
Because the Phantom Thieves suck at sneaking,
all their heists culminate in a climatic boss

00:12:08.949 --> 00:12:12.550
battle against the Palace’s owner, or at
least their Shadow.

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:16.959
These big bads are based on the Seven Deadly
Sins, with each of their Palaces explicitly

00:12:16.959 --> 00:12:19.459
named after one of the vices.

00:12:19.459 --> 00:12:20.459
1.

00:12:20.459 --> 00:12:24.439
Kamoshida, like many dudes who coach high
school girls’ athletics, is pervy; his Palace

00:12:24.439 --> 00:12:26.069
is the Castle of Lust.

00:12:26.069 --> 00:12:30.759
Inside it his Shadow looks like Asmodeus,
who, according to theologian Peter Binsfeld,

00:12:30.759 --> 00:12:33.180
is the Prince of Hell associated with Lust.

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:34.180
2.

00:12:34.180 --> 00:12:38.851
Madarama is an artist that uses other people’s
works to promote his own fame, so his Palace

00:12:38.851 --> 00:12:40.629
is the Museum of Vanity.

00:12:40.629 --> 00:12:41.629
3.

00:12:41.629 --> 00:12:46.160
Kaneshiro is a corpultant crime boss who hungers
for more and more money from those he extorts.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:50.509
That may sound like greed, but his palace
is the Bank of Gluttony, a theme reinforced

00:12:50.509 --> 00:12:55.470
not only by his rotundity, but by the Beelzebub-like
appearance of his Shadow, that being the demon

00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:57.459
Binsfeld connected to Gluttony.

00:12:57.459 --> 00:12:58.459
4.

00:12:58.459 --> 00:13:01.829
Futaba’s anger at herself for apparently
causing her mother’s death results in her

00:13:01.829 --> 00:13:04.179
Palace being the Pyramid of Wrath.

00:13:04.179 --> 00:13:05.179
5.

00:13:05.179 --> 00:13:09.920
Okumura is a businessman who envisions his
employees as robots existing only to labor

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:12.709
for him, his Palace being the Spaceship of
Greed.

00:13:12.709 --> 00:13:17.799
He isn’t interested in money solely, but
wealth in all its various expressions - i.e.,

00:13:17.799 --> 00:13:22.759
mammon, so it’s appropriate that the same
demon is also the name of his Shadow, again

00:13:22.759 --> 00:13:24.329
following Binsfeld’s list.

00:13:24.329 --> 00:13:25.329
6.

00:13:25.329 --> 00:13:29.819
Niijima is a prosecutor who’s envious of
her colleagues’ win records and thus willing

00:13:29.819 --> 00:13:31.939
to do anything to get a conviction.

00:13:31.939 --> 00:13:36.879
Her Palace is the Casino of Envy, where the
house always wins, and her Shadow - per Binsfield

00:13:36.879 --> 00:13:37.939
- is Leviathan.

00:13:37.939 --> 00:13:38.939
7.

00:13:38.939 --> 00:13:43.839
Shido is a politician who, when he tried to
force himself on a woman and Joker saved her,

00:13:43.839 --> 00:13:45.480
had Joker charged with assault.

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:50.549
His express aim as Prime Minister is to screw
over unwashed masses while profiting his chosen

00:13:50.549 --> 00:13:51.549
few.

00:13:51.549 --> 00:13:53.329
You know, a typical politician.

00:13:53.329 --> 00:13:57.230
His Palace is the Cruiser of Pride, traditionally
the deadliest sin.

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:58.230
8.

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:02.019
Humanity as a whole is responsible for such
intellectual and moral laziness that they

00:14:02.019 --> 00:14:06.199
collectively have a distorted perspective
of reality, leading to the public Palace known

00:14:06.199 --> 00:14:09.970
as Mementos, a.k.a. the Prison of Sloth.

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:11.850
And no, we didn’t forget how to count.

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:17.029
The Seven Deadly Sins have as their antecedent
the monk Evagrius Ponticus’ Eight Evil Thoughts,

00:14:17.029 --> 00:14:20.440
until Pope Gregory I subsumed Vainglory under
Pride.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:24.189
The ordering of the villains’ appearances
conforms roughly to the severity of the sins

00:14:24.189 --> 00:14:26.389
per traditional Catholic understanding.

00:14:26.389 --> 00:14:29.079
This is seen most vividly in Dante’s Purgatorio.

00:14:29.079 --> 00:14:34.930
Dante’s ordering was Lust, Gluttony, Avarice,
Sloth, Wrath, Envy, Pride.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:39.019
This is essentially the same as the order
of the Palaces in Persona, with one important

00:14:39.019 --> 00:14:44.670
difference: Persona moves Sloth to the final
slot, suggesting that Sloth is properly the

00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:46.079
deadliest sin.

00:14:46.079 --> 00:14:49.649
In addition to the inherent evil of their
signature sin, the villains are also ordered

00:14:49.649 --> 00:14:53.689
with respect to their sphere of influence,
with greater influence allowing for a greater

00:14:53.689 --> 00:14:55.859
severity to their transgressions.

00:14:55.859 --> 00:15:00.360
Whereas Kamoshida’s influence is limited
only to Shujin Academy, Madarame has influence

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:04.920
over the entire art community, Kaneshiro over
a wide swath of the criminal underworld, and

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:10.500
Okumura and Shido on a national stage as captains
of business and politics, respectively.

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:15.350
The final boss is Yaldabaoth, a gnostic name
for the creator of the world, because it wouldn’t

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:18.540
be a proper JRPG if you didn’t kill God
at the end.

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:22.209
And being God, his influence extends over
the whole of humanity.

00:15:22.209 --> 00:15:26.509
The name Yaldabaoth comes from the Apocraphon
of John: “Now the archon who is weak has

00:15:26.509 --> 00:15:27.509
three names.

00:15:27.509 --> 00:15:32.589
The first name is Yaltabaoth, the second is
Saklas, and the third is Samael.”

00:15:32.589 --> 00:15:38.000
This connects Yaldabaoth with the penultimate
boss, Shido, whose shadow is Samael and Joker

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:43.100
himself, as Saklas means “fool” a reference
back to Joker being on the Fool’s Journey.

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:46.549
Now the narrative progresses in one other
interesting way.

00:15:46.549 --> 00:15:50.769
The villains are ordered roughly according
to which system of ethics their supposed authority

00:15:50.769 --> 00:15:51.899
derives from.

00:15:51.899 --> 00:15:56.609
Kamoshida and Madarame are both adults in
a position of authority preying on high schoolers

00:15:56.609 --> 00:16:02.089
- Kamoshida by hitting on literal jailbait,
and Madarame by stealing his students’ artwork.

00:16:02.089 --> 00:16:04.920
Neither’s actions align with any ethical
theory.

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:08.410
Both simply presume that their age gives them
natural authority.

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:12.839
This is pretty much the first ethical framework
any individual operates under— to listen

00:16:12.839 --> 00:16:14.699
to those older than us.

00:16:14.699 --> 00:16:18.869
Kaneshiro’s self-loathing at his own perceived
weakness leads him to operate under the theory

00:16:18.869 --> 00:16:23.259
that might-makes-right, and to build a criminal
enterprise to compensate.

00:16:23.259 --> 00:16:26.889
All of these are what psychologist Lawrence
Kohlberg in his stages of moral development

00:16:26.889 --> 00:16:29.119
categorized as “pre-conventional.”

00:16:29.119 --> 00:16:34.269
Such moral attitudes are marked by their “deference
to superior power or prestige” as opposed

00:16:34.269 --> 00:16:36.359
to principled moral reasoning.

00:16:36.359 --> 00:16:41.079
Alternatively, as a prosecutor, Sae Niijima
occupies Kohlberg’s fourth stage of moral

00:16:41.079 --> 00:16:45.569
development, a “conventional” category
in which the law itself is the foundation

00:16:45.569 --> 00:16:49.199
for morality- whether or not the law is actually
just.

00:16:49.199 --> 00:16:54.199
Shido and Yaldabaoth represent Kohlberg’s
“post-conventional” stages of moral development.

00:16:54.199 --> 00:16:58.049
As Prime Minister, Shido’s authority derives
from the consent of the governed.

00:16:58.049 --> 00:17:01.819
This is Kohlberg’s fifth stage, in which
laws are malleable based on the will of the

00:17:01.819 --> 00:17:02.819
masses.

00:17:02.819 --> 00:17:07.650
Kohlberg’s sixth stage is that of universal
ethical principles - right and wrong are the

00:17:07.650 --> 00:17:12.699
same for all people at all places at all times,
regardless of man-made laws.

00:17:12.699 --> 00:17:17.270
One permutation of a universal ethical principle
is Divine Command Theory - the idea that the

00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:20.870
foundation of morality is whatever God says
is right or wrong.

00:17:20.870 --> 00:17:25.959
As a stand-in for God, Yaldabaoth is representative
of this type of moral reasoning.

00:17:25.959 --> 00:17:31.170
In fighting all these foes, the Phantom Thieves
are not merely opposing the deadly sins themselves,

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:35.060
but also the various ethical frameworks to
which society has subscribed.

00:17:35.060 --> 00:17:39.480
And we think this is why the structure of
the game imputes Sloth as the deadliest sin

00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:40.480
of all.

00:17:40.480 --> 00:17:44.180
Humanity’s sloth has made it intellectually
and morally lazy.

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:48.940
Humanity has abdicated the hard work of moral
decision making to these various ethical systems,

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:53.250
and the even harder work of actually being
morally active members of society, to those

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:58.020
few individuals running the various spheres
of influence - and unfortunately they’ve

00:17:58.020 --> 00:18:00.320
not been particularly moral.

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:05.600
The Thieves, while far from immoral or amoral,
don’t neatly conform their ethical hand-wringing

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:07.990
to any prescribed ethical theories.

00:18:07.990 --> 00:18:11.810
This is what differentiates them from the
slothfulness of the masses under the sway

00:18:11.810 --> 00:18:12.900
of Yaldabaoth.

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:16.380
Throughout all of the heists cumulatively,
the Thieves go through an ethical process

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:20.240
that French philosopher Jacques Derrida described
as “undecidability.”

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:24.900
Essentially, all moral decisions come down
to deciding between taking actions based on

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:30.220
a moral framework or rejecting those actions
for any reason ranging from not feeling like

00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:33.610
it to distrust for the moral frameworks at
play.

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:38.670
For instance The Thieves consistently reject
the justifications for the laws that Sae Niijima

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:39.710
blindly enforces.

00:18:39.710 --> 00:18:44.910
And even when the rules seem to have a foundation,
such as Shido’s democratic mandate or Yaldabaoth’s

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:50.330
divine commands, such rote formulae won’t
necessarily apply to individual circumstances.

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:55.790
Thus, according to Derrida, all moral decision
making is undecidable by prescribed ways of

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:56.790
thinking.

00:18:56.790 --> 00:19:00.750
“A decision that did not go through the
ordeal of the undecidable would not be a free

00:19:00.750 --> 00:19:06.920
decision, it would only be the programmable
application or unfolding of a calculable process.”

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:12.730
Only by exerting great moral and intellectual
effort - by continually undergoing Derridean

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:17.430
“undecidability” time and again throughout
their careers - are our heroes able to avoid

00:19:17.430 --> 00:19:19.330
the deadly sin of Sloth.

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:24.140
But while the Phantom Thieves avoided slothfulness
themselves, by being the only ones to take

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:28.980
on these various systems, they become a moral
crutch who everyone else outsources their

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:29.980
decision-making to.

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:34.060
So whether it’s the Thieves, or Sae and
Shido, the end result is the same.

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:38.530
This is why Yaldabaoth remains as powerful
as ever even after Shido is defeated.

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:42.260
At first, this seems to be an example of the
game’s mechanics coming into conflict with

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:47.210
its narrative – the story is saying that
society itself has to overcome its moral lethargy,

00:19:47.210 --> 00:19:51.480
but by virtue of being a game that can only
come about by decisions you as the player

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:57.740
make – the NPCs never make a real choice
and continue to avoid confronting undecidability,

00:19:57.740 --> 00:19:59.750
and continue being slothful.

00:19:59.750 --> 00:20:04.240
. Hiding the True Ending behind maxing out
all the Confidants is a smart solution to

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:05.240
this problem.

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:08.600
That is to say that in the True Ending all
of the NPCs who help with the final victory

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:12.670
have gone through the same ethical challenge
as The Phantom Thieves.

00:20:12.670 --> 00:20:17.190
Despite challenging such ethical frameworks,
by framing the decision to destroy Yaldabaoth

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:22.730
as unambiguously right, Persona 5 ultimately
affirms moral realism.

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:28.520
Even if no one ethical system can fully articulate
what makes good right and evil wrong, good

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:30.900
and evil are very much real.

00:20:30.900 --> 00:20:34.970
It condemns the moral nihilism of the game’s
foil, Goro Akechi.

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:38.800
This is a departure from Derrida, who rejects
the notion that we’re ever approaching a

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:43.700
True Ethics, and claims Undecidability is
the whole of the matter, but the game says

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:47.010
it’s only a step toward the truth of Right
and Wrong.

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:51.080
Thankfully, the game is more clear than real
life in assuring you that you did the right

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:55.810
thing, mainly by rewarding you with an anime
waifu on Valentine's Day.

00:20:55.810 --> 00:21:00.420
For balancing the complication of ethical
systems with an affirmation of moral realism

00:21:00.420 --> 00:21:05.721
and giving as extensive an examination of
moral wrongdoing as Dante, Persona 5 is as

00:21:05.721 --> 00:21:08.440
“Deep” as the Ninth Circle of Hell.

00:21:08.440 --> 00:21:09.790
But tell us what you think, Wisecrack.

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:14.640
Are we being too much like fortune-tellers,
reading too much into what’s just not there?

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:18.660
Or did we successfully infiltrate your cognition
and force a change of heart as to

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:20.160
how you feel about Persona 5?

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:22.470
Let us know in the comments below.

00:21:22.470 --> 00:21:24.090
Big shout out to all our awesome patrons.

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:28.100
Don’t forget to subscribe

